<title>USA: EMI unit sues Mosel Vitelic in patent dispute.</title>
<headline>EMI unit sues Mosel Vitelic in patent dispute.</headline>
<dateline>WILMINGTON, Del. 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>EMI Group Plc's U.S. unit is suing Mosel Vitelic Inc and its California subsidiary for alleged patent infringement.</p>
<p>In papers filed in the U.S. District Court in Delaware, EMI unit EMI Group North America Inc claims that integrated circuits made by Mosel infringe four EMI patents.</p>
<p>Those patents are for a CMOS susbstrate bias generator, a redundancy system for high speed wide-word semiconductor memories, an asynchronously equillibrated and pre-charged static RAM, and a multistage decoding technique.</p>
<p>EMI has asked for triple damages for alleged willful infringement.</p>
<p>Mosel Vitelic is a Taiwanese chipmaker.</p>
